      "id": "1408",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1408,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "The imperative or command form  (命令形) gives direct, blunt commands, e.g. 止まれ ('Stop!'). It can sound harsh unless softened with particles like よ, e.g. 頑張れよ ('Try harder, okay?'). In contrast, ことだ offers soft advice, e.g. 早起きすることだ ('You should wake up early.'), and is often used when giving recommendations or suggestions.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 1032,
          "slug": "命令形",
          "title": "命令形",
          "meaning": "(Verb)!, Do (something)!",
